"""Write SCREEN_NOTES.md from funnel.json and calibration.json (every number below is read from those files)."""
import json, os

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
F = json.load(open(os.path.join(HERE, "funnel.json")))
C = json.load(open(os.path.join(HERE, "calibration.json")))
fd = F["funnel_drawn"]
dn = F["dns"]
REQ = json.load(open(os.path.join(HERE, "request_counts.json"))) if os.path.exists(os.path.join(HERE, "request_counts.json")) else {}


def n(x):
    return "{:,}".format(x) if isinstance(x, int) else str(x)


def pct(a, b):
    return "%.1f%%" % (100.0 * a / b) if b else "n/a"


lines = []
A = lines.append
A("# Round 4 / B1: expanded blocklist stratum, screening notes")
A("")
A("Generated by `write_notes.py` from `funnel.json` and `calibration.json` (do not edit numbers by hand).")
A("Screening window (UTC): %s to %s. Vantage: the authors' residential connection in California." % tuple(F["screen_window_utc"] or ["?", "?"]))
A("")
A("## Status")
A("")
if F["target_reached"]:
    A("- Target reached: the drawn prefix holds **%d** stratum stores (target %d)." % (fd["candidates"], F["target"]))
else:
    A("- **Target NOT reached.** The screen stopped with **%d** stratum stores in an exact prefix of %s drawn domains "
      "(target %d). The prefix is still a simple random sample of the frame, so the list is usable as it stands; "
      "`screen.py` resumes where it stopped (see 'Resume')." % (fd["candidates"], n(F["drawn_prefix_n"]), F["target"]))
A("- DNS scan complete: %s (%s of 800,000 domains resolved in the contiguous prefix). Frame size N = %s%s." % (
    "yes" if dn["dns_scan_complete"] else "no", n(dn["domains_in_complete_prefix"]), n(F["frame_N_flagged"]),
    " (estimated from the scanned prefix)" if F["frame_N_is_estimate"] else ""))
A("")
A("## Files")
A("")
A("| File | What it is |")
A("|---|---|")
A("| `candidates.csv` | The stratum to measure: `store_id` (E-prefix, in draw order), `domain`, `rank`, `cmp`, `blocklist_readable`, `product_url`, `weight`, then diagnostics (draw order, pre-choice prediction for California, blocklisted ad vendors, CMP details, robots checks for the product page, age-gate hint, served title). RESTRICTED: contains domains. |")
A("| `blocklist_not_prechoice_ca.csv` | Drawn stores with a readable ad blocklist that their own configuration says is NOT applied before a choice in California. Not to be measured; descriptive only. RESTRICTED. |")
A("| `funnel.json` | All funnel counts, frame counts, weight. |")
A("| `calibration.json` | Static screen vs the main crawl's run-time reading on the 1,400 main-sample stores. |")
A("| `raw/dns_ext.csv` | DNS results for ranks 200,001-1,000,000 (compact; addresses kept only for flagged hosts). |")
A("| `raw/screen_results.jsonl` | One record per screened domain (stage, CMP evidence, blocklist entries). |")
A("| `raw/homepages/` | Gzipped homepage of every blocklist store; CMP script extracts of other target-CMP stores. Nothing else kept. |")
A("| `raw/vendor_cfg/` | Gzipped OneTrust / Cookiebot blocklist files for blocklist stores. |")
A("| `dns_scan_ext.py`, `screen.py`, `static_detect.py`, `robots.py`, `build_candidates.py`, `calibrate.py`, `write_notes.py` | Code. `dns_scan_ext.py` imports `sample/dns_scan.py`; `screen.py` imports `sample/verify.py` (eligibility, content screen) and `sample/build_frame.py` (platform list). |")
A("")
A("## Design")
A("")
A("- **List.** Tranco **L5PZ4** (the main sample's list, file already on disk), ranks **200,001-1,000,000** (800,000 domains).")
A("- **DNS flag.** Unchanged from the main sample (`sample/dns_scan.py`): apex or www resolves into 23.227.32.0/19 or CNAMEs to *.myshopify.com; Shopify platform domains dropped. At most 40 lookups in flight.")
A("- **Random order.** Domains were resolved in a seeded random permutation (seed 20260926). A flagged domain was screened only after every domain before it in the permutation had been resolved, so the screened set is always an exact prefix of a uniformly random order of the frame: a simple random sample without replacement.")
A("- **Draw.** The drawn set is the shortest prefix of the order that holds the target number of stratum stores; screened domains after it are `overdraw_not_in_sample` (as in the main sample). Design weight w = N / n = %s / %s = **%.4f** for every candidate." % (n(F["frame_N_flagged"]), n(F["drawn_prefix_n"]), F["design_weight"]))
A("- **Eligibility.** As in the main sample (`sample/verify.py`): HTTP 200; Shopify Online Store markers (headless excluded); no password page; adult/child keyword screen; product URL from the homepage. New: duplicates of main-sample or creator-stratum shops (same `Shopify.shop` or host) are excluded, and within the expansion the lowest-permutation domain of a shop is kept.")
A("- **Stratum definition.** An eligible storefront whose Pandectes, OneTrust or Cookiebot configuration publishes a readable blocklist that names at least one advertising vendor (`crawl/vendor_endpoints.json`) as blocked at least after a refusal, AND for which blocking before any choice for a California visitor is declared ('yes': Pandectes v4 ad category in `defaultBlocked`, or v5 with `USCA`/`US` in `regions.strict`) or can only be settled at run time ('unknown': OneTrust active groups, Cookiebot consent state). The rules mirror `crawl/build_tables.py:declared_by_vendor`, which defined the main paper's blocklist row. Stores whose configuration says the list is not applied before a choice in California ('no') are listed separately.")
A("- **Where the lists come from.** Pandectes: inline JSON in the homepage. OneTrust: `OtAutoBlock.js` named in the homepage, fetched once from cdn.cookielaw.org. Cookiebot: `configuration.js` for the page's `data-cbid` (or its California `data-georegions` id), fetched from consentcdn.cookiebot.com. These are the files every visitor's browser loads; vendor robots.txt was checked (both return 4xx = no restrictions).")
A("")
A("## Rules followed (ethics request section 5.1 / 5.2)")
A("")
A("- One `robots.txt` request and at most **one homepage GET** per store (redirects followed; the robots.txt of each new host was checked before each hop). RFC 9309 matching for product token `python-requests`; 4xx = allowed; 5xx/unreachable = skipped. No `products.json` request (unlike the main sample), so a store without a product link on its homepage has an empty `product_url`.")
A("- Default `python-requests` User-Agent (no spoofing), no cookies kept, no JavaScript, no retries, no forms, logins, carts or consent clicks.")
A("- Adult and child-directed stores: domain-name screen **before any request**; title/description screen on the fetched page; excluded, not reviewed by the student. Titles of adult-flagged pages were not stored.")
A("- Pacing: at most 1 homepage GET per second overall, at most 2 robots.txt GETs per second overall (different hosts), 6 sites in flight, vendor-CDN GETs at most 1 per second. Each store received at most 1 homepage request (plus redirect hops) during screening.")
A("- Storage: homepages kept only for blocklist stores (gzipped); free-disk floor 1.2 GB enforced by the screener.")
A("")
A("## Funnel (drawn prefix)")
A("")
A("| Step | n |")
A("|---|---:|")
A("| Tranco L5PZ4 ranks 200,001-1,000,000 | 800,000 |")
A("| Resolved (apex or www A record)%s | %s |" % ("" if dn["dns_scan_complete"] else " [scanned prefix]", n(dn.get("resolved", 0))))
A("| DNS-flagged Shopify (frame N)%s | %s |" % ("" if dn["dns_scan_complete"] else " [estimated]", n(F["frame_N_flagged"])))
A("| Drawn (exact random prefix) | %s |" % n(fd["flagged_drawn"]))
A("| Excluded before any request: adult / child domain name | %s / %s |" % (fd["excluded_before_any_request_adult_domain"], fd["excluded_before_any_request_child_domain"]))
A("| Skipped by robots.txt: unreachable / disallows `/` / redirect target | %s / %s / %s |" % (fd["skipped_robots_unreachable"], fd["skipped_robots_disallow_home"], fd["skipped_robots_redirect"]))
A("| Homepage fetched | %s |" % n(fd["homepage_fetched"]))
A("| ... of which fetched but record lost (nonresponse, not re-fetched) | %s |" % fd.get("fetched_but_record_lost_nonresponse", 0))
A("| HTTP 200 | %s |" % n(fd["http_200"]))
A("| Excluded: fetch error / non-200 / no Shopify markers / headless / password | %s / %s / %s / %s / %s |" % (fd["fetch_errors"], fd["http_non200"], fd["not_shopify"], fd["headless"], fd["password"]))
A("| Excluded: adult text / child-directed text | %s / %s |" % (fd["excluded_adult_text"], fd["excluded_child_text"]))
A("| Excluded: shop already in main sample / duplicate within expansion | %s / %s |" % (fd["dup_main_sample"], fd["dup_expansion"]))
A("| **Eligible storefronts** | **%s** |" % n(fd["eligible_storefronts"]))
A("| With Pandectes, OneTrust or Cookiebot detected | %s (%s) |" % (n(fd["with_target_cmp_detected"]), ", ".join("%s %s" % (k, v) for k, v in sorted(fd["target_cmp_detected_by_cmp"].items()))))
A("| Readable blocklist naming an ad vendor | %s (%s of eligible; by CMP: %s) |" % (fd["blocklist_readable_ad_vendor"], pct(fd["blocklist_readable_ad_vendor"], fd["eligible_storefronts"]), ", ".join("%s %s" % (k, v) for k, v in sorted(fd["blocklist_readable_by_cmp"].items()))))
A("| ... pre-choice in California: yes / unknown / no | %s / %s / %s |" % tuple(fd["prechoice_ca_among_readable"].get(k, 0) for k in ("yes", "unknown", "no")))
A("| Stratum store but product page disallowed by robots.txt | %s |" % fd["stratum_product_robots_disallowed"])
A("| **Candidates (`candidates.csv`)** | **%s** |" % fd["candidates"])
A("")
A("Other stages in the prefix: %s. Candidates by CMP: %s; by pre-choice prediction: %s; without a product URL: %s; with an age-gate hint (mentor to check): %s." % (
    ", ".join("%s %s" % (k, v) for k, v in sorted(F["stage_counts_drawn"].items()) if k.startswith("err_") or k.startswith("http_") or k.startswith("lost")) or "none",
    ", ".join("%s %s" % (k, v) for k, v in sorted(fd["candidates_by_cmp"].items())), ", ".join("%s %s" % (k, v) for k, v in sorted(fd["candidates_by_prechoice_ca"].items())),
    fd["candidates_without_product_url"], fd["candidates_age_gate_hint"]))
A("")
A("Screened beyond the prefix (overdraw, not in the sample): %s domains, %s of them stratum stores." % (n(F["overdraw_not_in_sample"]), F["overdraw_candidates"]))
A("Estimated stratum stores in the frame: %s; estimated stores with any readable ad blocklist: %s (w x count)." % (F["estimated_stratum_stores_in_frame"], F["estimated_readable_blocklist_stores_in_frame"]))
if REQ:
    A("Requests made by the screener (all runs): %s." % ", ".join("%s %s" % (k, n(v)) for k, v in REQ.items()))
A("")
A("## Validation of the static screen against the main crawl")
A("")
tab = C["agree_table_static_x_runtime_listed"]
A("On the %s main-sample stores, applying this screen to the homepages saved at sampling time (and the OneTrust/Cookiebot files the crawl captured):" % n(C["n_stores"]))
A("- Readable ad blocklist, static vs run time: both %s, static only %s, run time only %s, neither %s (sensitivity %s, no false positives)." % (
    tab.get("static=1,runtime=1", 0), tab.get("static=1,runtime=0", 0), tab.get("static=0,runtime=1", 0), tab.get("static=0,runtime=0", 0),
    pct(tab.get("static=1,runtime=1", 0), tab.get("static=1,runtime=1", 0) + tab.get("static=0,runtime=1", 0))))
A("  The misses are OneTrust stores whose `OtAutoBlock.js` is injected by script rather than named in the HTML, and one Pandectes store whose settings load from a file.")
sp = C["static_pre_x_runtime_pre_among_static_readable"]
A("- All %s stores of the paper's blocklist row (declared blocked before any choice at run time) are in the static stratum: 'yes' %s, 'unknown' %s." % (
    C["runtime_prechoice_blocked"], C["runtime_prechoice_blocked_by_static"].get("static_readable=1,static_pre=yes", 0), C["runtime_prechoice_blocked_by_static"].get("static_readable=1,static_pre=unknown", 0)))
A("- Static 'yes' was confirmed at run time on %s of %s; 'unknown' on %s of %s; static 'no' never showed pre-choice blocking (%s of %s)." % (
    sp.get("static_pre=yes,runtime_pre=1", 0), sp.get("static_pre=yes,runtime_pre=1", 0) + sp.get("static_pre=yes,runtime_pre=0", 0),
    sp.get("static_pre=unknown,runtime_pre=1", 0), sp.get("static_pre=unknown,runtime_pre=1", 0) + sp.get("static_pre=unknown,runtime_pre=0", 0),
    sp.get("static_pre=no,runtime_pre=1", 0), sp.get("static_pre=no,runtime_pre=1", 0) + sp.get("static_pre=no,runtime_pre=0", 0)))
A("")
# ---- expected yield at measurement (ratios from the main crawl, calibration.json)
yes_c = sp.get("static_pre=yes,runtime_pre=1", 0); yes_n = yes_c + sp.get("static_pre=yes,runtime_pre=0", 0)
unk_c = sp.get("static_pre=unknown,runtime_pre=1", 0); unk_n = unk_c + sp.get("static_pre=unknown,runtime_pre=0", 0)
cy = fd["candidates_by_prechoice_ca"].get("yes", 0); cu = fd["candidates_by_prechoice_ca"].get("unknown", 0)
exp_conf = (cy * yes_c / yes_n if yes_n else 0) + (cu * unk_c / unk_n if unk_n else 0)
A("## Expected size at measurement")
A("")
A("- Applying the main crawl's confirmation rates (static 'yes' %d/%d, 'unknown' %d/%d) to the %d candidates (%d 'yes', %d 'unknown') predicts about **%.0f** stores whose blocklist is in force before any choice at run time." % (yes_c, yes_n, unk_c, unk_n, fd["candidates"], cy, cu, exp_conf))
A("- In the main crawl, 7 of 21 such stores had the CMP itself write 'marketing: yes' without a click and left the primary analysis; at that ratio the primary (no-'yes') expansion sample would be about **%.0f** stores, added to the main study's 14." % (exp_conf * 14 / 21))
A("- The stratum is much rarer in ranks 200k-1M than in the main sample: most Pandectes installs there have the blocker switched off, and most OneTrust installs load no `OtAutoBlock.js`. The target of 250 stores (and 150+ primary) was therefore %s." % ("reached" if F["target_reached"] else "not reachable within this frame" if F.get("frame_exhausted") else "not reached when the screen stopped"))
A("")
A("## Deviations and incidents")
A("")
A("- **12 records lost (nonresponse).** In the first run (06:52-06:55 UTC, 27 Sep 2026) the stop path of `screen.py` discarded the results of 12 sites whose homepage had already been fetched once. They were not fetched again (one homepage request per site); they are in the drawn prefix as `lost_not_refetched` and treated as nonresponse. The bug was fixed before the restart (the stop path now drains and records every submitted site). Their note field in `raw/screen_results.jsonl` gives a wrong time (06:59-07:01); the correct window is 06:52-06:55 UTC.")
A("- The robots.txt rate was raised from 1 to 2 per second at the restart (different hosts each; homepage GETs stayed at 1 per second).")
A("- Unlike the main sample, no `products.json` request was made, so a candidate without a product link on its homepage has an empty `product_url`; the measurement crawl must resolve it within the per-site limit of 8 loads, or measure the homepage.")
A("")
A("## Limitations")
A("")
A("- Static screening misses blocklists that are only visible at run time (about 1 in 15 in the main sample: OneTrust auto-blocking injected by script; Pandectes settings loaded from a file). Those stores are outside the stratum as defined here, so the stratum is 'stores whose blocklist is visible in the served HTML or in the file it names'.")
A("- 'Unknown' pre-choice status (OneTrust, Cookiebot) is settled only by the measurement crawl; in the main crawl about half of such stores applied the list before a choice.")
A("- The adult/child screen is the main sample's keyword screen; no human review was done. Candidates with an age-gate hint are flagged for the mentor.")
A("- Weights assume one frame domain per shop; within-expansion duplicates were removed, but a shop reachable from two frame domains has twice the inclusion probability (rare; ignored).")
A("- One vantage point (California); no EU/UK run.")
A("")
A("## Resume / extend")
A("")
A("`python3 screen.py` (env `TARGET`, `WORKERS`) resumes from `raw/screen_results.jsonl` in the same random order; then `python3 build_candidates.py && python3 write_notes.py`. Any prefix is a simple random sample, so stopping early loses nothing but size. Stop a running screen with `touch STOP`.")
A("")
open(os.path.join(HERE, "SCREEN_NOTES.md"), "w").write("\n".join(lines) + "\n")
print("\n".join(lines))
